From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Milan Zamazal <mzamazal@redhat.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:40:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 19/29] libcamera: software_isp: Add autofocus controls

In order to support focusing operations, lens controls are set up and
passed around, similarly to the sensor controls.

Currently, the only control used, and only if the sensor supports
autofocus, is V4L2_CID_FOCUS_ABSOLUTE.  Instead of serializing the whole
lens ControList in setSensorControls, we could pass around just the
value.  But using the ControlList is more consistent with what we do
with the sensor controls and what is done in ipu3 pipeline.
Additionally, it's ready for possibly amending the controls in future;
we might end up having to determine between V4L2_CID_FOCUS_ABSOLUTE or
V4L2_CID_FOCUS_RELATIVE, or V4L2_CID_FOCUS_AUTO settings.

Signed-off-by: Milan Zamazal <mzamazal@redhat.com>
Link: https://patchwork.libcamera.org/patch/28732/
[Patrick: rebased on agc::prepareControls() taking the frame context]
Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
